1
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:35,100
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:39,100
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:43,100
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:48,100
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:51,100
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:54,100
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:57,100
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:57,100 --> 00:03:01,100
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:04,100
Now this exciting!

10
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:07,100
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:10,100
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:15,100
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:21,100
Separated from the rest of his crew,

14
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:24,100
Luffy launched a desperate attack on Navy Headquarters

15
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:27,100
in hopes of saving his brother from execution.

16
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:30,100
However, his struggle ended in vain,

17
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:33,100
with his enemies claiming an overwhelming victory,

18
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:35,100
along with Ace's life.

19
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:37,100
But this is a story from another time.

20
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:43,100
Ten years ago, in a corner of the East Blue, near Windmill Village.

21
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:46,100
Luffy, this here is Ace.

22
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:49,100
Anyway, you're gonna be living with him and Dadan from now on.

23
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:54,100
I know I was gone for a while, but I still wanna be friends!

24
00:03:54,100 --> 00:04:16,100
It's the end of the forest!

25
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:25,100
Here comes Sabo, the boy at the Great Terminal!

26
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:33,100
I can't believe we scored this much cash!

27
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:36,100
I told you, didn't I? Portume knows what's up.

28
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:38,100
Just tell him our treasure's from the Grand Line

29
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:40,100
and that greedy merchant can't help himself.

30
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:43,100
He was practically begging us for it.

31
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:47,100
If the dumbass wants to buy a bunch of trash we picked up on the shore,

32
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:48,100
I'm not gonna stop him.

33
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:50,100
Well, not like he's ever going to sea,

34
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:52,100
so it's all the same to him.

35
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:56,100
Not like we've ever been to sea either, though.

36
00:04:56,100 --> 00:05:12,100
What is this place?

37
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:17,100
On the north side of Mount Korvo, not far from where Dadan's bandits live,

38
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:20,100
there is a surprise at the end of the forest.

39
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:24,100
Covered in a thick mist, piles of trash reach toward the heavens.

40
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:28,100
It is a place where the unwanted gather.

41
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:32,100
That goes for the refuse, as well as those who reside there.

42
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:34,100
Rogues cast out by society.

43
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:37,100
It is a den of lawlessness.

44
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:39,100
Crime and disease run rampant,

45
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:42,100
with neither marines nor doctors present.

46
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:46,100
This place is known as Gray Terminal.

47
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:50,100
Hey Ace!

48
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:54,100
What the...

49
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:56,100
Oh...

50
00:05:56,100 --> 00:06:11,100
Wonder where he went.

51
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:19,100
Ace!

52
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:21,100
Stop trying to hide from me!

53
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:24,100
Come on!

54
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:29,100
Where are you?

55
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:31,100
Where are you?

56
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:39,100
Wow, I can't believe I slept all day again.

57
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:43,100
Just a bunch of junk.

58
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:45,100
Gotta be something.

59
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:47,100
Come on.

60
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:48,100
Tork it over!

61
00:06:48,100 --> 00:06:49,100
Yeah right!

62
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:50,100
That's mine!

63
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:51,100
Screw you!

64
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:52,100
I found it!

65
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,100
You're gonna break it, you idiots!

66
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:54,100
That's cool, man!

67
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:56,100
I just want to cash it in for you!

68
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:57,100
Yeah right!

69
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:59,100
Come on, just give me one pearl.

70
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:01,420
That's cool, man. I just want to cash it in for you.

71
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:04,620
Yeah, right. Come on, just give me one pearl.

72
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:14,100
Back off!

73
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:18,600
You can only blame yourself.

74
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:21,140
Next time, let's try this without all the running.

75
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:23,720
Look what I found.

76
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,420
No way.

77
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,100
Get back here!

78
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:30,100
Thief!

79
00:07:36,180 --> 00:07:38,400
Hey, move it, you brat.

80
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:41,320
What is your problem?

81
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,300
You want some of this?

82
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:45,040
He went that way!

83
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:45,540
Huh?

84
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:46,040
Uh...

85
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:46,540
Uh...

86
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:49,940
Uh...

87
00:07:49,940 --> 00:08:02,500
Eh...

88
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:26,580
Samo, hey, are you up there?

89
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,900
Oh, what's up, Ace?

90
00:08:31,740 --> 00:08:33,500
Sorry, I'm a little late this time.

91
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:34,540
More than a little.

92
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:38,180
I went out there and made a killing already today.

93
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,960
Oh, yeah?

94
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:43,760
Well, maybe I did, too.

95
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:44,740
Let's see.

96
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:48,820
Whoa, dude, you got more than me.

97
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:51,180
That's a ton of cash.

98
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:51,880
What happened?

99
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:56,420
Some chumps near the gate robbed them blind and made a run for it.

100
00:08:56,420 --> 00:08:57,920
Ha, well, crap.

101
00:08:58,220 --> 00:08:59,660
Guess you win again, buddy.

102
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:01,820
It doesn't matter if you win or lose.

103
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:05,060
We've got five years of pirate savings piled up.

104
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:07,500
We should both be happy about that.

105
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:12,840
We worked pretty hard.

106
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:15,220
Yeah, no kidding.

107
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:21,040
We'll leave this dump behind and go places these chumps never even dreamed of.

108
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:23,300
This is all going to be worth it.

109
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:24,440
Just you wait.

110
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:32,540
We'd better put it away now.

111
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:34,540
We can't let anyone else see this.

112
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:36,100
So how much is a ship?

113
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:38,620
I want a good one, but it seems like we're pretty rich.

114
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:41,080
Yeah, could take ten million.

115
00:09:41,460 --> 00:09:42,420
Maybe even more.

116
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:43,740
Shouldn't rush it.

117
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:45,580
Did you say ship?

118
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:47,440
You're going to be pirates?

119
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:49,920
And you've got hidden treasure already?

120
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:52,420
I'm going to be a pirate too!

121
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:04,980
Shut up!

122
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:09,380
You know what's cool?

123
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:12,680
Now that I know where you go, I can follow you every day.

124
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:13,420
Great.

125
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:15,120
Luffy, huh?

126
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:17,640
This is the brat you were talking about.

127
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:20,340
Does that mean he told your friends about me?

128
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:23,040
I was telling my friend how annoying you were.

129
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:26,120
He also told me that your head's full of rocks.

130
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,460
Head rocks!

131
00:10:28,660 --> 00:10:30,920
You do realize we're messing with you here, right?

132
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:33,840
The route I took here wasn't easy to follow.

133
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:37,380
I knew he was hard-headed, but I didn't think he was so tough.

134
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:39,720
So great that Ace has other friends too!

135
00:10:40,180 --> 00:10:41,900
I bet we're all going to be best pals!

136
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:43,140
I'm not your pal!

137
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:45,180
You don't even know my name, stupid!

138
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:47,400
Okay, then what is your name?

139
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:48,820
It's a secret!

140
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:51,360
I told you, didn't I?

141
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:52,560
You need to live here!

142
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:55,360
The mountains made you tough, but at this rate,

143
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:56,820
our whole plan's going to be ruined!

144
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:58,580
What now?

145
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:01,800
He knows our secret.

146
00:11:02,220 --> 00:11:04,580
We can't trust him to keep his mouth shut.

147
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:05,940
He's too stupid.

148
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:13,020
We'll kill him.

149
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:13,820
Yep.

150
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:15,160
Sounds good.

151
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:17,680
No!

152
00:11:20,060 --> 00:11:20,660
Stop!

153
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:21,580
This is scary!

154
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:24,100
Somebody help me!

155
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,720
I don't want to die!

156
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:26,720
Give me a break!

157
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:27,940
This kid is the worst!

158
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:29,160
Just kill him already!

159
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:29,980
Hurry it up!

160
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:31,340
He's your problem!

161
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:32,260
What are you doing?

162
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:34,480
Because I've never killed anyone before, okay?

163
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:35,860
Well, neither have I!

164
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,440
I don't know how this crap works!

165
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:38,840
Just don't throw me in the water!

166
00:11:38,980 --> 00:11:39,940
I'm begging you!

167
00:11:40,540 --> 00:11:41,660
Okay, the river!

168
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:44,220
That's convenient, but why did he say that?

169
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,400
I told you, he's stupid!

170
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:47,220
Somebody help me!

171
00:11:47,220 --> 00:11:48,220
Stop!

172
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:48,340
Stop!

173
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:48,640
Stop!

174
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,720
Don't kill me!

175
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:54,920
Wait, listen.

176
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:56,160
I just heard some screaming.

177
00:11:56,700 --> 00:11:57,620
Stop it, you kid!

178
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:58,560
Ah, damn it!

179
00:11:58,680 --> 00:11:59,680
Somebody hurt him!

180
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:00,760
Set him free.

181
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:02,380
We gotta get out of here and fast.

182
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:05,060
If people start snooping around, they'll find our treasure.

183
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,820
Sounds like you're talking about Ace and Sabo.

184
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:11,680
Those two are infamous around here.

185
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:14,140
And the one who took your money.

186
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:15,520
That was Ace, right?

187
00:12:15,660 --> 00:12:17,360
The kid who had the black hair, you said?

188
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:18,120
Uh-huh.

189
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:19,980
This is real pathetic, I know.

190
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,540
We both got sloppy.

191
00:12:21,540 --> 00:12:23,320
He's either cocky or dumb.

192
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:26,800
You can't rob pirates blind and expect to get away with it.

193
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:31,400
Bottom line is, if we don't get that money back, Captain Blue Jam's gonna skin us alive.

194
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:32,340
And I mean literally.

195
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:35,220
Blue Jam?

196
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:36,080
Crap!

197
00:12:36,420 --> 00:12:38,440
How was I supposed to know they were working with him?

198
00:12:38,820 --> 00:12:40,200
You robbed those guys?

199
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:42,140
Are you trying to get us killed or what?

200
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:42,940
Yeah.

201
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:45,140
This is not gonna end well.

202
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,120
That sword looks sharp.

203
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:48,820
Though you probably saw that already.

204
00:12:48,820 --> 00:12:51,920
The guy with him is Porchemy.

205
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:53,280
He's crazy.

206
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:58,800
Lose a fight with him, and he'll scalp you alive just to hear you scream.

207
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:04,940
Just lay low and let him pass by for now.

208
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:07,260
Uh-oh.

209
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:08,200
He's gone.

210
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:12,940
You've got to bring me down right now, you big-

211
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:14,600
How did you get caught already?

212
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:16,600
Wait, you want to play tough on?

213
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:17,820
Don't say I didn't warn you.

214
00:13:20,820 --> 00:13:22,460
Who the hell is this?

215
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:24,100
This guy won't put me down.

216
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:25,200
Ace, help!

217
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:28,640
Ace, why aren't you saving me?

218
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:29,420
We're friends, right?

219
00:13:29,420 --> 00:13:30,620
We should have killed him.

220
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:32,240
Now we're all dead.

221
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:32,840
Help!

222
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:32,960
Help!

223
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:50,680
So, you know Ace, do ya?

224
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:52,840
Yeah, that's right.

225
00:13:53,060 --> 00:13:55,460
And if you cry, do you think he'll come for ya?

226
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,840
Yeah, cause we're friends!

227
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:02,340
Except he just tried to kill me, so maybe not.

228
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:04,580
Shut up!

229
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:06,140
Are you kidding me?

230
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:09,200
If he's your friend, maybe you can help us.

231
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:10,820
See, Ace stole our money.

232
00:14:11,180 --> 00:14:13,980
And if we got it back, we wouldn't have to hurt anybody.

233
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:16,880
You don't happen to know where it is, do ya?

234
00:14:22,140 --> 00:14:23,020
We're screwed!

235
00:14:23,260 --> 00:14:24,960
They're gonna take our treasure for sure!

236
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:26,900
For once in your life.

237
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:27,940
Please shut up.

238
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:37,540
Well, are you gonna talk?

239
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:45,320
I don't know.

240
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:46,140
Sorry.

241
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:48,720
What a crappy liar!

242
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:58,340
All right, fine.

243
00:14:58,660 --> 00:15:00,480
I'm sure you just forgot.

244
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:07,320
Don't worry, I have ways of jogging your memory.

245
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:10,740
I told you, I don't know!

246
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:12,480
Let go of me, you dumb jerk!

247
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:14,900
Ace is gonna kick your butt, I'm telling you!

248
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,420
You're in big trouble, buddy.

249
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:17,480
You're gonna be sorry.

250
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:21,360
Okay, so now what?

251
00:15:21,660 --> 00:15:22,860
Stop asking me.

252
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:23,900
You know what.

253
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:33,940
Let me go!

254
00:15:34,340 --> 00:15:36,800
I'm not telling you a dark thing!

255
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:45,900
You little punk!

256
00:15:47,480 --> 00:16:04,420
The gum gum fruit turned me into rubber, so that stuff's not gonna work on me!

257
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:05,840
Calm down!

258
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:08,940
A devil fruit, huh?

259
00:16:09,620 --> 00:16:10,120
Hmm.

260
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:12,920
I know how to deal with that.

261
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:17,260
Bring me my pair of gloves.

262
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:18,820
Yes, sir!

263
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:20,520
Hurry, man!

264
00:16:20,740 --> 00:16:21,100
Faster!

265
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:22,980
We're screwed if those guys come back!

266
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,540
We gotta move all this.

267
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:25,760
But I don't know where.

268
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:30,100
Luffy's pretty stubborn, but it's only a matter of time before he rats us out!

269
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:33,560
I'm not losing our pirate savings to those jerks or anyone else!

270
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:35,720
It took us five years to score all this!

271
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:37,500
We can't get stuck in this dump forever!

272
00:16:43,020 --> 00:16:44,800
I'll try to clear this up a little.

273
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:47,760
The money Ace stole isn't just some chump change.

274
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:50,920
It's a matter of life and death for me and all of my buddies here.

275
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:53,420
